Stage 2c: climbable L2, pit death, rotation hint

Finishes the interrupted stage 2c work (75dc8bc was committed unverified) and
runs every acceptance check.

Fixed a call to a method that does not exist: _checkVoid set pitDeath and then
called this.die(), but the player's death entry point is kill(). Every pit fall
was throwing a TypeError instead of killing anything.

Pits are genuinely bottomless now, and this is where the brief's two statements
had to be reconciled. It asks for death at body.top < FLOOR_Y - 8 AND for the
pit's solid bottom to be gone, noting the player "dies before reaching it". With
the 30px body and the phantom solid tileAt reports below row 0, the body landed
at y=0 with its top at 30 and never crossed 24, so the first requirement could
not fire. tileAt now returns open below a hole column (holeCol, built by
ground()), so the body keeps falling and the -8 line is crossed. Every other
column keeps its phantom floor, and the level's outer edges stay solid.

Rotated rooms fall out in the current down direction. Physics runs in the
level's local frame, so "down" is a function of the rotation -- quarter steps
walk it through -Y, +X, +Y, -X. Level._syncDown records rotQ and which world
edge is open; tileAt opens that edge, _checkVoid tests the matching body edge,
and _clampToLevel no longer clamps it shut (it did, which made the rotated
death unreachable -- the body could never get past the edge to fall out of).
All three are recomputed after each quarter turn.

The void is drawn: a black quad under each hole at renderOrder 0, after the mid
trunks and before the tiles, so the pit no longer shows the parallax backdrop
through it and reads as ground you could land on. Anything that falls in is
removed, enemies included.

Rotation hint uses the real binding. The brief's example says R, but input.js
binds rotate to KeyE, so the toast reads "Pulsa E para girar el mundo" / "Press
E to turn the world". The controls screen already listed the rotate row with E.
Three runes sit three tiles before each hole in the L2 accent, one shared
material so they pulse together.

reach.mjs gained the two rules that exposed all of this: the required path
(spawn -> boss arena) solved with rises <= 40px, optional surfaces at <= 48px,
and wall occlusion, so a column taller than the jump now blocks the straight
path across it instead of being walked past in the graph. The required paths:

  L1  x0-61@32 -> x34-38@72 -> x44-49@80 -> x54-59@88 -> x66-71@96 ->
      x74-103@32 -> x84-90@72 -> x98-102@104 -> x108-113@80 -> x117-189@32
  L2  x0-29@32 -> x36-39@72 -> x54-61@32 -> x58-61@64 -> x65-67@32 ->
      x72-77@72 -> x84-101@32 -> x117-121@32 -> x118-120@72 -> x125-169@32
  L3  x0-43@32 -> x10-14@72 -> x18-22@96 -> x26-29@120 -> x34-38@144 ->
      x44-46@176 -> x54-59@72 -> x66-70@72 -> x74-77@96 -> x82-86@120 ->
      x92-94@160 -> x100-105@72 -> x112-139@32 -> x114-119@72 ->
      x124-128@96 -> x132-135@120 -> x143-179@32

L2 is the level the brief measured as stuck, and it is the one that needed
steps: five platforms in front of the five columns, and plat(72) lowered from
80 to 72 so the climb to the column at 82 is 40/16/40 instead of 48. The shard
that sat on the old height came down with it.

Acceptance: reach.mjs passes on all three (support 19/25/24, all surfaces and
all shards reachable, jump 131/132/90) and prints those paths. Two new tests
cover the void: dropped into an L1 hole Kael is dead and in the death state
after 1008ms with the red flash peaking at 0.35 and the fade bottoming at 0.05,
then the normal respawn returns control; and in a quarter-turned L2 the open
edge is the right one and falling out of it kills. Screenshots in
.scratch/stage2c/ (l2-column, pit-death, l2-hint) all read and checked by eye.
Zero console errors, and stage 2's story.mjs still passes 10/10.

