Committed as `d1fa07c` with the requested trailer. Stage 2c is complete and verified.

## What the WIP commit left broken

One call to a method that doesn't exist: `_checkVoid` set `pitDeath` then called `this.die()`, but the player's death entry point is `kill()`. **Every pit fall was throwing a TypeError instead of killing anything.** Everything else from the WIP (L2 steps, void quads, runes, hint, new reach rules) was in place.

## A genuine conflict in the brief

§2 asks for death at `body.top < FLOOR_Y - 8` **and** for the pit's solid bottom to be removed, noting the player "dies before reaching it". Those can't both hold as written: with a 30px body, the phantom solid below row 0 catches the fall at `y=0`, so `top=30` and the line at 24 is never crossed — exactly the "Kael just stands in the pit" symptom. I made the hole columns genuinely open (so the body keeps falling and the −8 line is crossed) and kept the phantom floor everywhere else. Flagging it because it's me resolving an inconsistency in the spec, not just implementing it.

Rotated rooms needed a second fix: `_clampToLevel` reset any X past the edge, so the rotated death was **unreachable** — the body could never get out to fall. That edge is now left unclamped, which is the whole point of it being open.

## Acceptance — all run, all read by me

**`tools/reach.mjs` passes on all 3 levels**, required paths printed:

```
L1  x0-61@32 -> x34-38@72 -> x44-49@80 -> x54-59@88 -> x66-71@96 ->
    x74-103@32 -> x84-90@72 -> x98-102@104 -> x108-113@80 -> x117-189@32
L2  x0-29@32 -> x36-39@72 -> x54-61@32 -> x58-61@64 -> x65-67@32 ->
    x72-77@72 -> x84-101@32 -> x117-121@32 -> x118-120@72 -> x125-169@32
L3  x0-43@32 -> x10-14@72 -> x18-22@96 -> x26-29@120 -> x34-38@144 ->
    x44-46@176 -> x54-59@72 -> x66-70@72 -> x74-77@96 -> x82-86@120 ->
    x92-94@160 -> x100-105@72 -> x112-139@32 -> x114-119@72 ->
    x124-128@96 -> x132-135@120 -> x143-179@32
```

Support 19/25/24, all surfaces and all shards reachable, jump 131/132/90. L2 got five steps in front of its five columns, and `plat(72)` lowered 80→72 so that climb is 40/16/40 instead of 48.

**Playwright pit-death check:** dead and in the death state after **1008ms** (limit 1500), red flash peak 0.35, fade bottomed at 0.05, then the normal respawn returns control. Plus the post-rotation L2 case: `rotQ=1`, open edge `{"right":true}`, falling out kills.

**Screenshots in `.scratch/stage2c/`** — all three read: `l2-column.png` (Kael on the step at y=72 with the column beside him), `pit-death.png` (flash + fade, "Has caído", Kael below the floor in a black void with the lip either side), `l2-hint.png` (toast + two purple runes before the hole). Zero console errors. `tools/story.mjs` still passes 10/10 after the player/physics/level changes.

Two things to be aware of:

- **The rotate key is `E`, not `R`.** The brief's example text says R, but `input.js` binds `rotate: ['KeyE']`, so the toast reads "Pulsa E para girar el mundo" / "Press E to turn the world". The controls screen already listed the rotate row with `E`, so nothing needed adding there.
- **`pit-death.png` holds the fade/flash at a fixed point** (fade 0.5, flash 0.3) for the capture. The real fall-out is 0.4s of fade after a 0.12s flash, and that window is shorter than a screenshot round-trip on the software rasteriser — my first two attempts both caught a frame after the sequence had already finished. Only the two `postUniforms` setters are overridden, in the capture script; no game code is affected.
