Stage 2d: panels 07-10 in the deal and theft

The WIP commit for this stage (8945d07) turned out to contain only
.bunny-loop.log, so none of the work had been done; this is all of it.

PANEL_IDS now lists 07 through 10 alongside 01-06, so they are preloaded with
the rest when a new game starts. Verified by watching the network: all ten
cutscene images are requested on "Nueva partida" and none fail. The new files
are JPEG data under .png names, which the browser handles; they are used as
they are, not renamed or converted.

Only the `show` column moved. The text is untouched, still all from
strings.js, in both languages.

The deal now runs level, 03, 07, 08, 04, 04, 09 -- so the first line is
portraits over the level with no still, three of the seven lines get their own
new art, and 04 is left carrying the two lines that were already its business.
The theft moves its second narration to 10 and leaves Kael's line on 06.

One thing that needed no change: the `isPanelId` test is /^[0-9]{2}$/, which
already matches '10', and the CSS rule that gives a real still a dark backdrop
keys off data-art^="0" plus a data-art^="1" exception for 'kael', so 10 lands
on the dark field rather than one of the legacy colour gradients.

Acceptance: tools/story.mjs passes 10/10, exit 0, zero console errors, and the
three checks that name a panel still find them (04 on Kael's line in the deal,
06 on Kael's line in the theft). Screenshots of 07, 08, 09 and 10 in
.scratch/stage2d/, all read: 07 is the elder as a hooded merchant with a pack
and staff, 08 opens the bag of gold and jewels under a reaching gauntlet, 09 is
Kael from behind watching the lantern walk away, and 10 is the wide one of the
elder at the wall with the shadow behind him -- narration, so no speaker name,
which matches the brief's "—" on that line. tools/reach.mjs still passes too.

